# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# OzBridge is maintained by a single person, so one catch-all rule is the
# whole truth: every path has the same owner. Per-directory rules would
# only imply a team split that does not exist — add them here if and when
# the project gains maintainers.
#
# The practical effect is on external contributions: any PR from someone
# other than the owner auto-requests their review. GitHub never requests
# review from a PR's own author, so this stays quiet for the maintainer.
